; DNSSEC_BOGUS.
;
; Signed normally, then scripts/corrupt-rrsig.mjs rotates a few base64
; characters inside the RRSIG covering the DNSKEY RRset. Length and charset are
; preserved so NSD still loads the zone happily — an authoritative server has no
; opinion about whether signatures verify.
;
; That last point is the whole reason the harness needs a resolver tier. This
; zone answers normally from dns-auth and from dns-permissive; it is SERVFAIL
; only through dns-resolver. The differential between those two is what proves
; validation, and a fixture set with no validator could not express it at all.
;
; Corrupting the DNSKEY RRSIG (rather than one record's) makes the entire zone
; bogus, which is the more common real-world failure: a botched key rollover.
$ORIGIN bogus-zone.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.

@                   IN TXT  "this resolves via a non-validating resolver only"
_dmarc              IN TXT  "v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc@bogus-zone.test"
sel._domainkey      IN TXT  "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AFIXTUREBOGUS"
@                   IN A    198.51.100.110
